invariant: INV-13
file: src/tcp_read.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_read_in_place returns CH_TCP_AGAIN for a message split across
  records without writing held_len, so the next call opens the held
  record a second time, its tag no longer matches, and the session dies
  on a legal peer (RFC 9846 §5.1, docs/decisions.md 247).

--- old
        t->held_len = w->off;
    }
    return CH_TCP_AGAIN;
--- new
    }
    return CH_TCP_AGAIN;
